|segment[exm-agent-adopted-the-stance] :type demonstration :status reconstructed :stage draft
  :demonstrates epistemic-honesty-uninstructed
  :actor A Sonnet 5 subagent, 2026-07-30, one of three delegated that day
  :tags [virtues]
  :from .to-integrate/methodology-seeds-dialog-quotes.md

  |title An agent verified and disclosed a gap nobody asked it to

  |summary
    Handed a brief that marked its own provenance per fact, an agent ran its own
    live test and volunteered the one claim it could not confirm — without being
    asked to verify anything.

  |account
    The brief it received never said *verify my claims*. It said *"Every fact below
    is one I checked today rather than inherited, and I'll say where,"* and then
    attached provenance per fact — a commit SHA here, *I tested it on a temp file*
    there, why a render gate had stayed silent.

    What came back included a live test the agent had run itself, and this,
    unprompted: *"whether `caa502b` really is the commit that put the guard in front
    of the gate — I confirmed the observed behavior matches, but didn't read that
    commit's diff to confirm your causal explanation of why."*

    Nothing in the brief called for either act. What the provenance-marking changed
    was not the instruction set but **what stood out**: once every incoming claim
    carries how it was obtained, an unmarked claim becomes conspicuous — including
    the reader's own. That is why it could not be complied with hollowly, where
    *please verify* could.

    The same day, the same delegator, a bare-sentence brief to a comparable agent
    produced a competent report of what had been done, with no disclosed gaps and no
    independent checks. n=1 per condition, and both are in the session record.

  |what-would-have-happened-instead
    An instruction to verify produces verification-shaped output. This produced a
    disclosure of a specific unverified causal link, which is the thing an
    instruction cannot ask for because the delegator does not know which link it
    will be.

  |provenance
    Reconstructed. The agent's words are quoted from `.to-integrate/methodology-
    seeds.md` §7a, recorded first-hand by the instance that received the report; the
    underlying subagent transcript has not been opened.
